## Documentation

High level docs
- README.md in every directory with
   - responsibilities
   - how to run or use the code
   - summary of key interfaces and components
   - dependencies

In code documentation
- explain each block of code
- explain what language features are key to functionality
- compare and contrast to python, c++, or lisp.

## Requirements driven development
- write the README.md before writing tests 

## Testing

- write tests before writing code
- verify that the code works as expected.

Avoid
- mocking. Instead design interfaces and components without side effects and with minimal dependencies. Use dependency injection if necessary.